title: Authorizations › Case page › Source chip
route: /authorizations/case/R-1042?tab=draft
intro: The small source chips on the draft, the clinical picture and the criteria. Clicking one opens the page of the chart it points to in a side panel, with the sentence the agents used boxed.
dir: TD
also: Demo only: the 'page' is a short generated sheet with the quoted sentence. The full document stays in the chart system.
---
group gW "Where chips appear"
  screen w1 "Clinical picture & draft › each draft section\nEach sentence from an applied action adds its own"
  screen w2 "Clinical picture rail › diagnosis and medications"
  screen w3 "Criteria & risk › inside each criterion, beside the quoted chart text"
endgroup
click c "Click a source chip\ne.g. 'Psychiatric eval p.1'"
overlay m "Side panel titled with the source name\n'J.M., 34 · R-1042'"
doc d1 "Sheet 'Source document'\n'Privacy mode: names, dates of birth and member IDs masked'"
doc d2 "Facts on the sheet\nPatient, Payer, Level of care, Request"
doc d3 "The quoted sentence, boxed and highlighted"
agent rd "Reader read the chart\nIntegrity checked each sentence against it\n(demo: the quote is stored text)"
decision dY "Is it a chip for an answer you typed?"
process yo "Chip reads 'Your answer'\nQuote: 'Typed by you for Scribe on this request.'"
click x "Click the X"
click dim "Click the dimmed area"
click esc "Press Esc"
end e "Side panel closes\nYou are back on the same tab, nothing changed"

w1 --> c
w2 --> c
w3 --> c
c --> m --> d1 --> d2 --> d3
d3 -.-> rd
c --> dY
dY -->|Yes| yo
m --> x --> e
m --> dim --> e
m --> esc --> e
